<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a three-stage tree calculation</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(cx=0)"]]A farmer plants three bean seeds. Each seed germinates with probability \({@p@}\), independently.[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]Three boda boda riders pass a checkpoint. Each rider wears a helmet with probability \({@p@}\), independently.[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]Chebet takes three free throws in a basketball match. She scores each with probability \({@p@}\), independently.[[else]]A school buys three solar lamps. Each lamp works for a year with probability \({@p@}\), independently.[[/if]] Wafula worked out the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]exactly two seeds germinate[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]exactly two riders wear a helmet[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]she scores exactly two[[else]]exactly two lamps work[[/if]]. He wrote S for success and F for failure. His working has one mistake.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid #999;padding-left:10px;">[[if test="is(er=1)"]]<p>Paths: SSF.</p><p>\(P = {@p@} \times {@p@} \times {@1-p@} = {@v@}\)</p>[[elif test="is(er=2)"]]<p>Paths: SSF, SFS, FSS, SSS.</p><p>\(P = 3 \times {@p@} \times {@p@} \times {@1-p@} + ({@p@})^3 = {@v@}\)</p>[[else]]<p>Paths: SSF, SFS, FSS.</p><p>Each path \(= {@p@} \times {@p@} \times {@p@} = {@p^3@}\).</p><p>\(P = 3 \times {@p^3@} = {@v@}\)</p>[[/if]]</div><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) What did Wafula do wrong?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the correct probability.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Exactly two successes happen on three paths, SSF, SFS and FSS. On each path the two S branches have probability \({@p@}\) and the F branch \({@1-p@}\), so each path has probability \({@p@} \times {@p@} \times {@1-p@} = {@p^2*(1-p)@}\). The three paths are equal, so multiplying one by 3 is right.</p><p>(a) [[if test="is(er=1)"]]Wafula used only one of the three paths.[[elif test="is(er=2)"]]Wafula included SSS, which has three successes, not exactly two.[[else]]Wafula used \({@p@}\) on the F branch, where the item fails; that branch has probability \({@1-p@}\).[[/if]]</p><p>(b) \(3 \times {@p^2*(1-p)@} = {@ta2@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
